  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    The Promenade Ward is a commercial and residential district within Aurora Stack, centered on a main gallery lined with merchant stalls, fire-core braziers, and the star-channeling spires designed by Summit-Lord Yahailong, the colony's founding leader. It has served as an epicenter for both the Gilding and the Accord — the Ward's principal trade festivals — and for the Collapse that nearly destroyed it. The Ward trades in aurora-light and ambition. The ledgers record the former more honestly than the latter.
    
    ## Infrastructure
    
    Yahailong's star-channeling spires are set at fractionally different angles, cascading aurora-light downward through the galleries in measured waves. Three fire-core braziers line the main promenade: two along the eastern approach, one at the gallery junction. The eastern quarter's heating runs on a sixteen-core heat-conductor lattice installed during the founding's first season, its crystalline housing bedded directly into the ice.
    
    The lattice was designed for sixteen cores. The founding-era shipment records log fourteen. The discrepancy — two cores diverted by Yahailong to construct western perimeter heat-barriers against orca scouts — cost two families their lives during the third winter. The families Moqai and Xuelin froze. Yahailong subsequently altered the ice-memory using Snowdrift-numb techniques taught to her by Hainou mewei'Frostglass, an Aurora Stack merchant instrumental in the Ward's founding. A memorial wall near the western approach bears carved names of settlers lost in those early winters; the count it preserves does not include Moqai or Xuelin. Those with access to records kept outside the Ward's ice-memory have noted the discrepancy. The shadow-ledgers, recovered by the researcher Zhinghoua lang'Gleam, confirm it.
    
    The eastern gallery mouth accommodates four penguins abreast before narrowing to two where old ice-supports jut inward — a bottleneck that has cost lives during every evacuation since reconstruction.
    
    ## The Collapse and Recovery
    
    In the cycles preceding the Collapse, stockpiled aurora-crystals had been threaded through the merchant quarter until it blazed with refracted light. The star-channeling spires pulsed past design tolerance. The fracture that followed ran through the merchant quarter in patterns that looked almost intentional. During the worst of the subsequent Thaw, two of the three braziers were found cold, their cores deliberately pulled by someone who understood the mounting brackets well enough to conceal the timing.
    
    Three conflicting testimonies survive from the period surrounding a major ice-fracture during the Tide Custom festival: civic recorder Lianheizhi attributed it to geological chance; Stack soldier Skael'Frost described a deliberate confiscation ordered by Plunge-Caller Oeichowei, the Ward's controversial authority figure; Nightshelf emissary ☽'velumae testified that a Crypt-seal artifact buried beneath the promenade had been corrupting the deep ice for weeks. The three accounts are mutually exclusive. No cross-examination was convened.
    
    The Ward recovered. Qingfu'spire, the research faction that originated here, maintains laboratories along the promenade. Trade flows again under the restored Accord.
    
    ## The Deep Ice
    
    Beneath the promenade lies a trading-floor level where aurora-light enters at angles the surface galleries cannot catch — visible from below, invisible from above. Below that, fourteen corruption-threads were found during the Thaw radiating outward through the deep ice beneath the eastern walkway: claw-width fissures in a pattern the Nightshelf calls warning and the Stack calls background noise.
    
    Graffiti on the eastern spire reads *'Oeichowei walked here,'* scratched deep enough to survive refreezing. Locals do not acknowledge it. No one has painted it out.
